    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="0562" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.24/88: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-22T13:00:00-04:00">August 22, 1941—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>208. Your 357 August 20, 6 p.m. In view of the fact that the financial terms vary
                    from country to country the Department would not welcome publication of the
                    various texts which would permit comparison <pb facs="0563" n="555"
                        xml:id="pg555"/> of the financial terms offered the several American
                    republics. Nevertheless, if the proper Uruguayan procedure requires a general
                    congressional discussion of the matter, and since the secret cannot be properly
                    guarded, the Department authorizes you in your discretion to agree to the
                    publication of the text of the agreement.</p>
                <p>The Department is sending you a revised text of the Lend Lease Agreement which
                    contains no changes of substance, but a number of modifications of form to make
                    mutual the undertakings of Articles 4 and 5 and the suspension of deliveries
                    clause of Article 1 (text of July 26 Instruction<anchor n="12" xml:id="d457-f1"
                    />). A parallel text has already been sent to Rio de Janeiro, and the Department
                    is requesting the Embassy there to telegraph it to you at once.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
